{{!-- /the-faith-received/connections/ — the citation atlas, ported.

     THE CORPUS SITE'S /web INSIDE THIS SITE. Same shape as the ported
     reader and library: his engine (web.in02.js, shelf-constellations.js,
     connection-evidence.js), our shell. It extends `default`, so our
     masthead and footer wrap it and Ghost owns the document. What went is
     the page's home link and the bridge bar back to his site; what stayed
     is its own bar: the page name, and the mode navigation (Explore ·
     Paths · Topics · Shelf maps · Scripture) that web.in02.js drives.
     Every byte of data comes from the library worker on R2: the graph,
     the reception shards, the rooms. Nothing here reaches Blob.

     THE BODY CLASS. constellations.css lays the whole atlas out from
     body.web-page and the mobile explorer/map switch keys on
     body[data-view]. Ghost renders <body class="">; the boot script
     below sets both before this markup parses. The atlas is a
     full-viewport instrument (body overflow hidden), as it is on the
     corpus site; faith-port-surfaces.css starts it under our masthead. --}}
{{!-- THE GATE (Ian, 2026-09-24: "Anywhere any one of these tools shows
     up ... they need to be met with a subscribe pop-up"). Connections is
     a research tool, so this page gates the way /compare/, /desk/ and
     /search/ do: a signed-in member (free included, during the beta) is
     served the atlas; anyone else gets the hero and the beta gate, and
     the tfr-connections modal opens over it on arrival
     (a hidden span carrying data-gate-on-arrival, read by feature-gate.js;
     hidden and empty because the click gate would otherwise catch every
     click inside it, the beta gate's own form included). /web/ and
     /constellations/ render this template, so they are gated with it.
     The doors to this page elsewhere are gated by their address in
     feature-gate.js; this covers a direct visit or a shared link.

     The rail sits outside the condition, one instance, so a signed-out
     reader still has the rest of the library. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-tfr-rail.js"}}" defer></script>
